          "headline": "The first elected Bangsamoro Parliament chooses Macacua as chief minister",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The first elected Bangsamoro Parliament convened October 30 in Cotabato City and chose Abdulraof Macacua as chief minister, 51 votes to 27 for Ahod Ebrahim. The 80-member house ends seven years of appointed transition rule. It is the first elected parliament for the Bangsamoro region, a milestone for Muslim Filipino self-governance and representation.</p>",
